  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Reyhanli Transshipment Support to Partners on Cross Border Activity through the provision of necessary logistics services and oversight coordination</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">ltpgtltbrgtThe mandated tasks for the Logistics Cluster under the Consent Based Agreement implies the Cluster to perform crucial key activities planned for this period including continued support for cross border operations from T&#xfc;rkiye. The Cluster will continue supporting cross-border activities from T&#xfc;rkiye into the northern parts of Syria by facilitating access to free-to-user transshipment services at Bab al-Hawa to the humanitarian community. Priority will be given to make use of local available logistics capacity and advocate for the pooling of resources among partners when and where possible. To complement the cross-border operation, the Logistics Cluster will work on improving the customs services related to the exportation of humanitarian assistance from T&#xfc;rkiye to Syria through its partnership with the Turkish Customs Authorities. Ensuring the continuity of cross-border logistics support is a critical priority for the Logistics Cluster in the July-December period. The transshipment hub in Reyhanli Turkey&#xa0;serving UN agencies plays a critical role in facilitating the timely and cost-effective delivery of humanitarian aid into Aleppo and Idlib. Preserving this cross-border mechanism is vital to maintaining a streamlined, collaborative, and impactful humanitarian response in one of Syria&#x2019;s most vulnerable regions.lt/pgt</narrative>
  </description>
